      "text": "Blue Lake Cave and the Sucuri River"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "823e945b37490fd15358b1fce4f74d452afe932e7936dec214701ad4f1bc7881",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261107-6cc062915871",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, visit Blue Lake Cave. The cave is known for its geological features and deep blue water. Sunlight reaches into the cave, and the water changes colour with the light. Blue Lake Cave is one of the world’s largest flooded caves.\n\nIn 1992, an expedition of Brazilian palaeontologists discovered fossil remains of prehistoric mammals at the bottom of the cave, including giant sloths and sabre-toothed tigers.\n\nAfter lunch, the programme continues on the Sucuri River, where you’ll snorkel in crystal-clear water. The river is so clear that you can see underwater plants and wildlife up to 50 metres away. As you swim, you’ll see aquatic plants and fish around you, and the current lets you take in the underwater world at an easy pace."
    },
